    <string name="help_fallback_purpose">Choose DIRECT or a selector for the current subscription’s final MATCH rule. Keeping the original leaves it unchanged.</string>
    <string name="help_fallback_scenarios">Use it for connections that matched no earlier rule. Hidden selectors remain available.</string>
    <string name="help_fallback_cautions">It applies after local routing and scripts. An invalid target resets only after the complete candidate is saved.</string>
    <string name="help_geo_purpose">Manage GeoIP, GeoSite and ASN data and select the format and loader for runtime configurations.</string>
    <string name="help_geo_scenarios">Update, import or restore the bundled snapshot. Install GeoIP.dat before selecting DAT mode.</string>
    <string name="help_geo_cautions">Files are verified before replacement. A running session keeps its snapshot until it restarts.</string>
    <string name="help_routing_purpose">Compose ordered local groups, retain each enable state and set the rule strategy and final MATCH.</string>
    <string name="help_routing_scenarios">Append before terminal rules, prepend or rebuild routing. Proxy rules use the selected local selector.</string>
    <string name="help_routing_cautions">Rebuilding requires an enabled local selector and an explicit MATCH. Disabled references retain dependencies.</string>
    <string name="help_display_purpose">Set node density, order, test concurrency and connection handling after node changes.</string>
    <string name="help_display_scenarios">Large, medium and small show one, two and three nodes per row. Large text reduces the column count.</string>
    <string name="help_display_cautions">Latency and current-node data come only from the matching running session. Offline candidates never invent test results.</string>
    <string name="help_package_purpose">Import or export desktop Jeemi versioned JSON packages containing a local configuration and its full dependency graph, or one script.</string>
    <string name="help_package_scenarios">Use packages to share routing plans. Import previews list additions, replacements and affected subscriptions.</string>
    <string name="help_package_cautions">The library changes only after confirmation and validation of all affected subscriptions. A changed library requires a new preview. Desktop packages include enabled custom fields; disabled field drafts stay on this device.</string>
    <string name="help_appearance_purpose">Choose a light, dark or system theme and an application language.</string>
    <string name="help_appearance_scenarios">These preferences apply to all four pages. Save to apply them, or cancel to keep the previous selection.</string>
    <string name="help_appearance_cautions">Theme and language changes preserve the resource library. Language also follows the Android application language setting.</string>
